# The workflow's `run:` blocks execute in bash on a Linux runner. If they are
# checked out with CRLF, every line ends in a stray \r and the shell fails with
# errors like `$'\r': command not found`. Force LF on everything the runner or
# a POSIX shell touches. The .bat files are Windows-only, so they keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
